From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ThreadedCompositor::releaseMemory: dispatch asynchronously to avoid main-thread stalls

Upstreamable WebKit fix (not POWER-specific; WebKitGTK 2.54.3):

LayerTreeHost::releaseMemory(WTF::Critical) calls
ThreadedCompositor::releaseMemory(critical) during memory-pressure sweeps
even when MemoryPressureHandler requests asynchronous release. Because
ThreadedCompositor::releaseMemory() uses m_workQueue->dispatchSync(), the
main thread blocks on BinarySemaphore::waitUntil() whenever the compositor
thread is busy painting a complex frame, turning a slow frame into a main-thread
hang and WatchDogQueue crashAfter10Seconds() SIGABRT.

releaseMemory() returns void and only invokes
PlatformDisplay::sharedDisplay().skiaReleaseUnusedResources(critical) on the
compositor work queue while holding protectedThis = Ref { *this }. Dispatching
asynchronously via m_workQueue->dispatch() eliminates the main-thread stall
while preserving work-queue execution order (including before
ThreadedCompositor::invalidate()'s synchronous drain).

--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp
@@ -877,7 +877,7 @@ void ThreadedCompositor::fillGLInformation(RenderProcessInfo&& info, CompletionH
 
 void ThreadedCompositor::releaseMemory(WTF::Critical critical)
 {
-    m_workQueue->dispatchSync([protectedThis = Ref { *this }, critical] {
+    m_workQueue->dispatch([protectedThis = Ref { *this }, critical] {
         PlatformDisplay::sharedDisplay().skiaReleaseUnusedResources(critical);
     });
 }
